        "body": "In the forests of central Finland, Soviet divisions advanced along narrow roads where vehicles could not easily maneuver. Finnish ski troops split long columns into isolated pockets called mottis, then destroyed them piece by piece.\n\nA Legendary Finnish Victory: The battles of Suomussalmi and Raate Road became symbols of Finnish skill and Soviet failure. Small Finnish units defeated much larger formations by exploiting winter, terrain, local knowledge, and Red Army confusion.",
