        "body": "Finland's resistance drew wide sympathy in Europe and the United States. Newspapers celebrated Finnish courage, volunteers traveled from neighboring countries, and aid campaigns raised money and supplies, though direct military help remained limited.\n\nSoviet Union Expelled: The League of Nations condemned the invasion and expelled the Soviet Union in December 1939. Britain and France considered intervention through Scandinavia, but plans were slow, politically complex, and never arrived before the war ended.",
