    "slides": [
      {
        "title": "A Harsh Peace",
        "body": "The Moscow Peace Treaty ended the war on 13 March 1940. Finland ceded the Karelian Isthmus, Viipuri, territories around Lake Ladoga, and other areas. The price was severe, but Finland remained independent.\n\nEvacuation and Loss: Hundreds of thousands of Finns left ceded territories rather than live under Soviet rule. The territorial loss became a national wound and shaped Finland's next decisions as Europe moved deeper into World War II.",
        "img": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Moscow_Peace_Treaty_1940_map.svg",
        "cap": "Territories ceded by Finland after the Winter War",
        "stats": [
